  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Intermittent light rain showers, possibly mixed\nwith snow, will impact areas north of Bangor through Wednesday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA weak low pressure system over Quebec will track E towards the\nstate today. Precip is expected to begin in the afternoon with\nmainly rain/snow mix in the north and rain in the south. Cannot\nrule out a light accumulation of snow in the North Woods. By\ntonight, chances of snow showers in the north increases, though\naccumulation will still be light. By Wednesday, remaining\nmoisture, shortwave energy, CAPE values around 50 J/kg, and\nsteep lapse rates will aid in the development of isolated\nshowers throughout the day. High res models indicate that the\nsnow showers should stay north of the Bangor Region and be a mix\nof rain showers and snow showers depending where and when the\nconvective initiation is. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Potential for coastal storm development later in\nthe week. However, significant uncertainty still exists.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nLow pressure will develop along the Mid-Atlantic coast \nThursday. This initial low will then track northeast Thursday\nnight into the weekend. A second low should then develop Friday\nand also track northeast into Saturday. However, significant \nuncertainty regarding the tracks of these lows still exists. \nPotential impacts from these lows, including precipitation \ntypes/amounts, Thursday night into the weekend will be dependent\non the eventual tracks of these lows.",
